A choice defines a value that takes one of several named forms.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    WindowEvent = {
        Opened,
        Resized | width I32, height I32 = 720 |,
    }
]

`Opened` carries no data. `Resized` uses the same field list as a struct.
Its constructor needs a width and uses a height of 720 when the caller omits it.
Both variants produce a `WindowEvent`.
